<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Texuandri</h1><p class="st-meta">50 BCE – 350 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">People of the sandy heathlands of the Kempen and Brabant whose land, Toxandria, became the first Roman foothold of the Salian Franks.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Known chiefly from Pliny, who lists them among the peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-belgica">Gallia Belgica</a>, the Texuandri lived in the region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a>, in the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campine">Belgian Kempen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-brabant">North Brabant</a>. They may have been a subdivision of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tungri">Tungri</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their rulers. Their land was thinly settled, with scattered farms on poor sandy soils, and inscriptions record Texuandrian soldiers serving in the Roman army, including in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 3rd and 4th centuries the area was disrupted by Frankish raids. In 358 the future emperor Julian accepted the submission of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/salian-franks">Salian Franks</a>, who had already settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toxandria">Toxandria</a>, and let them stay as Roman allies, and the region became the cradle of Frankish power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 50 BCE – 350 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:58.71%;width:7.96%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>50 BCE – 350 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a>, <a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Toxandri</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=texuandri" aria-label="Texuandri on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4812 376 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Texuandri lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5132 632h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5132 632h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Netherlands. <a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=texuandri">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

